35,2,1,talk,Jonathan,,The ledger shows our development allocation is down by nearly a quarter this year.,"{""words"":14,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
36,2,1,talk,Shion,,"The call-back trial cut readmissions by a fifth, but only while it was running.","{""words"":14,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
37,2,1,talk,Midori,,"The therapy review shows four years of physiotherapists leaving, but midwifery has slack.","{""words"":13,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
38,2,1,talk,Kenji,,"The booking system has no slot for walk-ins, and the car park is full by eleven.","{""words"":16,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
39,2,1,talk,Shizue,,The board minutes show a joint clinic closed in a year because no one owned the rota.,"{""words"":17,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
40,2,2,talk,Jonathan,,"@Shion, that readmission drop is good, but it stopped when the trial ended.","{""words"":13,""mentions"":[""Shion""],""raw_differs"":false}"
41,2,2,talk,Shion,,"@Jonathan, yes. It proves the model works, but it also proves it needs a permanent home.","{""words"":16,""mentions"":[""Jonathan""],""raw_differs"":false}"
42,2,2,talk,Midori,,"@Shizue, that joint clinic failure is exactly what I fear. Who will own the new rota?","{""words"":16,""mentions"":[""Shizue""],""raw_differs"":false}"
43,2,2,talk,Kenji,,"@Midori, if the car park is full, the new patients cannot even get to the door.","{""words"":16,""mentions"":[""Midori""],""raw_differs"":false}"
44,2,2,talk,Shizue,,"@Midori, I agree. The data agreements with outside surgeries took fourteen months to sign.","{""words"":14,""mentions"":[""Midori""],""raw_differs"":false}"
45,2,3,talk,Jonathan,,The tariffs are the key. On-site sessions bill at the standard outpatient rate.,"{""words"":13,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
46,2,3,talk,Shion,,The booking system records only named slots. Unrecorded work vanishes from the reports.,"{""words"":13,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
47,2,3,talk,Midori,,The midwifery slack is real. We could absorb the new program without agency cover.,"{""words"":14,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
48,2,3,talk,Kenji,,"The shuttle misses fifteen villages. If the program is for them, it will not reach them.","{""words"":16,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
49,2,3,talk,Shizue,,The outside surgery agreement is the bottleneck. It will take fourteen months to sign.,"{""words"":14,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
50,2,4,talk,Jonathan,,So the on-site model is the only one that earns back its cost.,"{""words"":13,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
51,2,4,talk,Shion,,The unrecorded work is the real problem. We need a system that captures it.,"{""words"":14,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
52,2,4,talk,Midori,,The midwifery slack is the only staffing pool that can absorb the new program.,"{""words"":14,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
53,2,4,talk,Kenji,,The car park and shuttle are the real barriers. We need to fix the access first.,"{""words"":16,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
54,2,4,talk,Shizue,,The outside surgery agreement is the real bottleneck. We need to sign it before we start.,"{""words"":16,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
